{
 "format": "feir.approval-assertion",
 "version": 1,
 "owner": "feir-os",
 "wire_format": "feir.tenant-assertion v1",
 "generator": "scripts/vectors/gen_approval_assertion.py (independent Python reference, stdlib only)",
 "spec": [
  "Wire format: the tenant assertion (feir.tenant-assertion v1, vectors/tenant-assertion.v1.json) in X-Govder-Tenant-Assertion, keyed with M (VULTRINO_APPROVAL_ASSERTION_SECRET), never with F.",
  "Request: POST /api/v1/approvals/<id>/decision, no query, where <id> is the approval id path-escaped once (Go url.PathEscape: every byte outside [A-Za-z0-9-._~] and outside the sub-delimiters $&+:=@ is %XX with uppercase hex). The signed path is that single-escaped path, exactly as transmitted.",
  "Body: Go encoding/json of {approve, approver, approver_class (omitted when empty), note} with keys sorted, compact, '<' '>' '&' U+2028 U+2029 escaped as \\u003c \\u003e \\u0026 \\u2028 \\u2029. The MAC binds these exact bytes, so the approver subject and class cannot change after signing.",
  "vultrino verifies against the raw request-target it received (OriginalUri), the Host header, the exact body, the tenant of the tenant-scoped admin key (expected_tenant) and a TTL ceiling of min(assertion_ttl, 300 s)."
 ],
 "consumers": [
  "feir-os app/internal/planes Vultrino.DecideApproval (producer: the request it transmits)",
  "vultrino src/govder/tenant_assert.rs verify_tenant_assertion (verifier on POST /api/v1/approvals/{id}/decision)"
 ],
 "reasons": {
  "bad_mac": "no accepted key produces the MAC for the received request",
  "wrong_tenant": "the assertion names a tenant other than the admin key's"
 },
